<title>GERMANY: Bilfinger 4-mo construction output rises.</title>
<headline>Bilfinger 4-mo construction output rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four months to April 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group construction output		2,834   up 11.4 pct</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic output			   1,394   up 8.6 pct</p>
<p>     Foreign output			    1,440   up 14.3 pct</p>
<p>    Group new orders			   2,829   down 5.1 pct</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic new orders		     1,109   up 6 pct</p>
<p>     Foreign new orders			1,720   down 11.1 pct</p>
<p>    Group orders in hand		     9,975   up 2.6 pct</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic orders in hand		 3,927   down 14.2 pct</p>
<p>     Foreign orders in hand		  6,048   up 17.5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German construction group is Bilfinger + Berger Bau AG. The group said it planned to concentrate full-year 1997 construction output growth in its foreign business. It said the fall in domestic new orders was due to weakness in the German economy. Bilfinger said that while new orders in the first quarter were down, it had received two large contracts in Thailand and Nigeria in April 1997.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
